course: dictionary
lesson: 13929
title: Who makes the laws?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A legislator is a person who makes laws. The word has two parts: legis- means law, and -lator means a person who does a job. Clues in the sentences help too: «The legislators voted to make school free for all.» Voting is part of making laws, so a legislator is someone who helps decide the rules a country or state must follow.
explain: Look for clues about place and work. «Our local legislators meet in the town hall once a month.» Local tells you they come from your area, and meet in the town hall tells you they work together as a group. Legislators are not just people who talk about laws. They help write and vote on them.
explain: You will often find this word in news reports, history books and formal writing. When you see it, ask: who decides the rules here? If the answer is a group of elected people, the word is probably legislators.
fact: A legislator is a person who makes laws.
fact: Legislators belong to a parliament, a congress or another law-making group.
fact: «Legislator» is a formal word, so you will often find it in news reports and history books.
fact: In the USA, a member of Congress or a state legislature is a legislator.
fact: In the UK, MPs and members of the House of Lords are legislators.
exercise: «The legislators voted to make school free for all.» What did the legislators do? | Cooked lunch for the school | Went home early | Painted the classroom walls | *Made a new law by voting
exercise: What does legislator mean? | A person who teaches maths | *A person who makes laws | A person who checks the weather | A person who looks after lost animals
exercise: «Our local legislators meet in the town hall once a month.» Find and copy one word that tells you the legislators come from the same area. | once | meet | *local | month
test: «Legislators must read a law carefully before they vote.» What must legislators do before they vote? | Skip the law and vote at once | *Read the law carefully | Leave the room | Sing a song about it
test: In the UK, which people are legislators? | *MPs and members of the House of Lords | Police officers only | Shopkeepers and bus drivers | Doctors and nurses only
exam: Which word fits best? «The ___ voted to change the law on parks.» | Teachers | Pilots | *Legislators | Bakers
